hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2830","Narrated to us Ali ibn Muslim, narrated to us Khalid ibn Makhlad, narrated to us Ali ibn Salih, on the authority of Maisarah ibn Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal ibn Amr, on the authority of Sa'id ibn Jubayr (RA), who said:\n\nWe were with Ibn Abbas (RA) at Arafah when he said to me, \O Sa'id"," why do I not hear the people saying the Talbiyah?\""\n\nI replied"," \""They fear Mu'awiyah.\""\n\nSo Ibn Abbas (RA) left his tent and said"," \""Labbayka Allahumma labbayk (Here I am"," O Allah"," here I am). Verily"," they have abandoned the Sunnah out of hatred for Ali.\""\n\nAbu Bakr (RA) said: The reports from the Prophet (ﷺ) indicate that he continued to say the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamrah. This clarifies that he used to say the Talbiyah at Arafah.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""
